Aims to provide and improve treatment services for patients afflicted with Alzheimer´s disease by authorizing the DOH to give grants to public and non-profit private health care providers.

Enumerates conditions for grant to recipients such as:
 
a) a comprehensive approach to Alzheimer´s care that integrates treatment of patients with training and support services for their families/caregivers;

b) services shall be provided in the dialects or languages and cultural backgrounds most appropriate for of the patients to be served; 

c) provision of outreach activities to inform the public on Alzheimer´s disease and of the services of the program.

Seeks to promote the rights and interests of the paying consumer-subscriber by mandating telecommunications company to act with fairness and equality by providing for quality services, resources management, service regulation, penalties-sanctions and dispute resolution.

Penalizes the telecommunications company/service provider who violates or who fails to comply with this Act:
a)	First Offense - a fine of not less than Two hundred thousand pesos (P200,000.00);
b)	Second Offense - a fine of not less than Five hundred thousand pesos (P500,000.00);
c)	Subsequent Offenses - a fine of not less than One million pesos (P1,000,000.00) and revocation of the franchise to operate.

Aims to give certain classes of senior citizens graduated discount which will amend specifically Sec. 4 of R.A.9994 on the grant of 20% discount.

Provides for:  TWENTY PERCENT (20%) discount for those who are 60 - 70 years old;
THIRTY PERCENT (30%) discount for those who are 70 - 80 years old;  
FORTY PERCENT  (40%) discount for those who are 80 - 90 years old; and
FIFTY PERCENT (50%) discount for those who are 90 years old or over.

Seeks to amend some provisions of Republic Act No.10912 with the following provisions:

a) That registered and licensed professional are exempted from compliance within the FIRST FIVE YEARS after obtaining their licenses;

b) That failure to comply with CPD shall only be a basis to deny renewal of Professional Identification Cards after the lapse of the compliance period; 

c) That licensed Professional OFWs shall be exempted from the requirement for the period of their overseas employment; and

d) That professionals shall only be required to obtain a maximum of 36 CPD credit units once every five years.

Seeks to provide all officers and members of our Barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan
with just and proportionate allowances and benefits as follows:

Punong Barangay - Not less than THREE THOUSAND PESOS (P3,000.00) per month;

Sangguniang Barangay Members, Barangay Treasurer and Barangay Secretary -
Not less than THREE THOUSAND SIX HUNDRED PESOS (P3,600.00) per month;

Sangguniang Kabataan Secretary, Treasurer and Members - Equivalent to ONE HALF (1/2) of the monthly allowances and benefits received by the Sangguniang Kabataan Chairman.
